# Lands entering at the same time as Haunted Ridge are not "other lands you control" for it (CR 614.12, 101.4; the ruling): it
# looks at the battlefield as it was before the event. In turn 5 Bot1 cracks Flooded Strand for an Island and Strip Mines its own
# Haunted Ridge, and Second Sunrise (Black Lotus's white) returns the Ridge, Strip Mine, Flooded Strand and the Lotus together:
# Bot1 controlled only the Island before, so the Ridge enters tapped though three other lands are on the battlefield after.

[Bot1 Deck]
Haunted Ridge
Strip Mine
Flooded Strand
Black Lotus
Second Sunrise
Mountain
Mountain
Mountain x3
Island
Mountain x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x18

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Haunted Ridge.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Strip Mine.Play
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Flooded Strand.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Flooded Strand.Activate
Bot1.Search(Island)
Bot1.Battlefield.Strip Mine.Activate(Bot1.Battlefield.Haunted Ridge; Ability: Destroy)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield = Island
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: White)
Bot1.Hand.Second Sunrise.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield = Island; Haunted Ridge; Strip Mine; Flooded Strand; Black Lotus
Bot1.Battlefield.Haunted Ridge.Tapped = true
Bot1.Battlefield.Strip Mine.Tapped = false
Bot1.Battlefield.Flooded Strand.Tapped = false
